INSERT INTO settings (key, value) SELECT 'terms_text', replace('Effective November 3, 2026. These Terms are an agreement between you and USMLE100 LLC ("USMLE100", "we", "us") for use of usmle100.com and the USMLE100 student portal. You accept these Terms, the Refund Policy and the Privacy Policy by ticking the agreement box when you create your account, and the Student Agreement by signing it in the portal. We keep a dated record of the exact version you accepted. Section 20 requires individual arbitration of most disputes; you may opt out within 30 days.\n\n## 1. Who can use USMLE100\n\nYou must be at least 18 years old. Each account is for one named person. You must give accurate details when you register (name, email, phone number, exam and graduation year) and keep them up to date.\n\n## 2. What we provide\n\nUSMLE100 is exam preparation for USMLE Step 1, COMLEX and CBSE. Each program runs for 100 days: 90 weekday lecture days taught live over Zoom, followed by a 10-weekday exam window. Programs include lecture recordings, a question bank and study tools; some programs also include Evening Questions classes, the USMLE100 Course Book and one-on-one tutoring. What each program includes is listed on the Programs page at the time you buy.\n\nUSMLE100 is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Federation of State Medical Boards (FSMB), the National Board of Medical Examiners (NBME), the NBOME or any exam provider. We do not guarantee any exam result or score. Our content is for exam preparation only and is not medical advice.\n\n## 3. Prices and payment\n\nPrices are shown in US dollars on the Programs page. Current prices: MedSchool Refresher $1,500; MedSchool Companion $1,999; MedSchool Complete $2,449; MedSchool MAX $3,799; one-on-one tutoring $50 per 60-minute session; Evening Questions $160 per month (bought one month at a time; it does not renew automatically); Course Book $199. Payments are processed by Stripe; we never see or store your full card number. Your program is activated once Stripe confirms the payment. Each payment page states that continuing to payment means you accept the Terms and Refund Policy then in force (all sales final), and we record that acceptance.\n\n## 4. Refunds\n\nAll sales are final, except as the Refund Policy and section 9 (ending access for a reason that is not your breach) state.\n\n## 5. Your account and devices\n\n• One person, one account. Your account may be used only by you, and you may hold only one account. You may not share, lend, transfer or sell your account, login, password, sign-in codes or access to anyone, including family, friends or classmates. Sharing your account can lead to a permanent ban without refund and legal action (see section 9 and the Student Agreement).\n\n• Your account works on up to 2 registered devices. A third device, or a replacement device, needs approval from USMLE100. Clearing your browser data or using private browsing can make a device look new.\n\n• Only one lecture can play at a time on your account.\n\n• If we detect the same account playing lectures in two places at once, we record a warning. A second occurrence locks the account until USMLE100 reviews it.\n\n• Five wrong passwords within 15 minutes lock the account until USMLE100 unlocks it.\n\n## 6. Lecture recordings and viewing limits\n\n• Recordings stream inside the portal only. They cannot be downloaded.\n\n• Each lecture can be watched twice per enrollment. A viewing is used once you have watched 90% of the lecture, or 24 hours after you first press play, whichever comes first. Within those 24 hours you can pause, end the lecture and come back without using another viewing.\n\n• If a technical problem interrupts a viewing, your progress is kept and you can continue where it stopped. A technical problem does not by itself give back a viewing.\n\n• Once both viewings of a paid lecture are used, you may ask in the portal for one additional viewing, and you may dispute a viewing you believe was counted in error through My account → Appeals and disputes. USMLE100 decides each request at its discretion.\n\n• Free lectures can be watched twice, on the same terms; additional viewings are not available for free lectures.\n\n• Recordings are available until 60 days after the last day of your program (Day 100). After that, access ends.\n\n• Your name, account number and a session code appear on the video while you watch.\n\n## 7. Acceptable use\n\nYou must not: record, capture, photograph, download, copy, share, sell, publish or redistribute any lecture, question, Course Book page or other material; try to get around the viewing limits, watermark, device limits or other protections; share your account; or use the service to harass others or post unlawful content in Ask the Room. The Student Agreement sets out these rules in more detail.\n\n## 8. Intellectual property\n\nAll lectures, live classes, recordings, questions, explanations, the question bank, the Course Book, slides, software and website content belong to USMLE100 LLC or its licensors and are protected by copyright, trade-secret and other laws. Your purchase gives you a limited, personal, revocable, non-transferable licence to view them for your own study during your access period. The licence ends automatically if you break these Terms or the Student Agreement, or when your access ends. No other rights are granted. The watermark, viewing limits, device limits, encryption and sign-in checks are technological measures that protect copyrighted works; getting around them is a breach and may also violate federal law (17 U.S.C. § 1201). "USMLE100" and our logos are our trademarks.\n\n## 9. Suspension and termination\n\nSuspension. We may suspend your account, or any part of your access, immediately and without notice whenever we reasonably suspect account sharing, copying, recording, unauthorised access, circumvention of our protections, payment fraud or a serious breach of the Code of conduct. During a suspension we review our records (sign-ins, devices, viewing, watermark and payment records), and you may respond through My account → Appeals and disputes.\n\nTermination for breach. If our review finds, in good faith, that you broke these Terms or the Student Agreement, we may end your access permanently and close any other accounts you hold. You will not receive a refund. Our decision after review is final, subject only to section 20.\n\nTermination for other reasons. If we end your access for a reason that is not your breach (for example, if we stop offering a program), we will refund the unused part of what you paid, in proportion to the days of access remaining.\n\nLegal remedies. If you record, copy, download, share or sell USMLE100 content, or share your account, we may also take legal action for a court order to stop it (an injunction) and for damages, and seek our reasonable attorneys'' fees, costs and other enforcement expenses wherever a statute, court or arbitrator allows (Student Agreement section 5.2). Chargebacks are covered in section 19.\n\n## 10. Changes\n\nWe may update these Terms. We will post the new version with its effective date and, for material changes, tell you through the portal. If the Student Agreement changes materially, you will be asked to sign it again before continuing.\n\n## 11. Disclaimers and limitation of liability\n\nThe service is provided "as is". To the fullest extent the law allows, USMLE100 is not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential losses, and our total liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. These limits do not apply to losses caused by our fraud, gross negligence or wilful misconduct, or to any liability that cannot be limited by law.\n\nNo guarantee of results. Your exam result depends on many things outside our control, including your own study, attendance, health and the exam itself. USMLE100 does not promise, guarantee or warrant that you will pass any exam, reach any score, match into any residency or obtain any licence, and nothing said in classes, marketing or testimonials is such a promise.\n\nExam results. You agree that not passing an exam, receiving a particular score, not matching or being dissatisfied with your results is not, by itself, a basis for any claim, refund, compensation or damages against USMLE100. This does not take away any right that the law does not allow to be waived.\n\nNo other liability. To the fullest extent the law allows, USMLE100 is not liable for lost earnings, lost opportunities, exam or application fees, travel, or any indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss. The cap above, and its exceptions, apply to every claim.\n\nIndemnity. If someone else brings a claim against USMLE100 because you copied, recorded, shared or sold USMLE100 content, shared your account, posted unlawful material, or otherwise broke these Terms or the law, you will reimburse USMLE100 for the resulting reasonable losses and costs, including reasonable attorneys'' fees where the law allows. This does not cover claims caused by USMLE100''s own fault. We will tell you about the claim promptly.\n\n## 12. Governing law and contact\n\nThese Terms are an agreement between you and USMLE100 LLC. They are governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina and applicable US federal law (including the Copyright Act), without regard to conflict-of-law rules. The Federal Arbitration Act governs section 20. Questions and legal notices: info@usmle100.com.\n\n## 13. No bots, scraping or AI training\n\nYou may not use bots, scrapers, download tools, browser extensions or automated means to access, copy or collect any content, or use any USMLE100 content to train, fine-tune or feed an artificial-intelligence model or tool. You may not reverse engineer, probe or try to break the site''s security or protections.\n\n## 14. Confidential materials\n\nQuestions, explanations, the Course Book and lecture content are confidential and proprietary. Posting or describing them on forums, social media, group chats or question-sharing sites is a breach of these Terms. You must also never share actual exam questions from the USMLE, COMLEX or any other licensing exam, here or anywhere.\n\n## 15. Live classes and recordings\n\nLive classes and tutoring sessions may be recorded by USMLE100 and made available to students. By joining, you consent to being recorded, including your name, voice, video and chat messages. Only USMLE100 may record classes; you may not record them yourself.\n\n## 16. Schedule and content changes\n\nWe may change instructors, reschedule classes, skip holidays and update or replace course content to keep it accurate. Such changes do not entitle you to a refund unless a material part of what you bought is not delivered (Refund Policy section 2). We are not responsible for delays or interruptions caused by events beyond our reasonable control, including internet, platform or power outages.\n\n## 17. Your posts and feedback\n\nYou keep ownership of what you post in Ask the Room, but you give USMLE100 a free, permanent licence to use, display and edit it within the service. Feedback and suggestions you send us may be used freely. We will only publish a testimonial with your name if you agree.\n\n## 18. Monitoring and evidence\n\nYou agree that USMLE100 monitors viewing, sign-ins, devices and account activity to protect its content and accounts, as described in the Privacy Policy. We may keep and use these records, and the watermark on any copied material, as evidence in an investigation, chargeback, takedown, arbitration or court case, for as long as that matter lasts.\n\n## 19. Chargebacks\n\nPlease contact us before disputing a charge. You keep any right the law or your card issuer gives you to dispute a charge. If you dispute a charge for a purchase you authorised and received, we may suspend access to that purchase while the dispute is open, give the card issuer our records (including your acceptance of these Terms and your sign-in and viewing history), and seek to recover any amount wrongly reversed. A dispute decided in our favour restores access.\n\n## 20. Disputes\n\nInformal resolution first. Before starting any claim, you must email info@usmle100.com describing it and give us 30 days to try to resolve it.\n\nBinding arbitration. Except as stated below, any dispute between you and USMLE100 arising from these Terms, the Student Agreement or the service will be decided by final, binding, individual arbitration under the Consumer Arbitration Rules of the American Arbitration Association, held in North Carolina or by video, and not in court. USMLE100 pays the fees those rules assign to the business. The arbitrator may award any individual relief a court could award, including attorneys'' fees and costs only where the law allows. The arbitrator decides questions about the scope and enforceability of this section, except that a court decides the class-action waiver.\n\nNo class actions. Claims may be brought only individually, never as part of a class, collective or representative action. If this waiver is found unenforceable for a claim, that claim is decided in court, not in class arbitration.\n\n30-day opt-out. You may opt out of arbitration by emailing info@usmle100.com within 30 days of creating your account, giving your name, account email and a statement that you opt out. Opting out does not affect the rest of these Terms.\n\nCourt exceptions (both sides). Either you or USMLE100 may (a) bring an individual claim in small-claims court if it qualifies, and (b) go to court for an injunction or damages for infringement, misappropriation or misuse of intellectual property, circumvention of technical protections, or unauthorised account access. This includes USMLE100''s claims against anyone who copies, records, shares or sells its content.\n\nVenue. Any case heard in court will be heard only in the state courts located in North Carolina or the federal district courts of North Carolina (which hear copyright claims), and you agree to their jurisdiction.\n\n## 21. General\n\nThese Terms, the Refund Policy, Privacy Policy and Student Agreement are the whole agreement between you and USMLE100 LLC. If a court or arbitrator finds any part unenforceable, that part is limited to the extent necessary and the rest still applies. Our not enforcing a term is not a waiver. Sections on intellectual property, confidentiality, acceptable use, suspension and termination, monitoring and evidence, indemnity, liability, chargebacks and disputes survive termination, expiration, refund or chargeback. Electronic agreement: ticking the agreement box and typing your name to sign are electronic signatures with the same effect as handwritten ones (federal E-SIGN Act; North Carolina Uniform Electronic Transactions Act), and you may ask us for a copy of what you accepted. You agree to receive notices electronically, by email or in the portal. We may transfer these Terms to a successor business; you may not transfer them.\n\n## 22. Statements about USMLE100\n\nYou may share your honest opinion of USMLE100. You may not:\n\n• make false statements of fact about USMLE100, its owners, instructors or staff, or anything defamatory;\n\n• harass, threaten or abuse USMLE100 staff or other students, online or offline;\n\n• pretend to be USMLE100, an instructor or staff member, or claim to speak for USMLE100;\n\n• post or quote USMLE100 content (lectures, questions, explanations, Course Book pages, screenshots) while doing so;\n\n• publish other students'' personal information.\n\nWe ask that you contact us at info@usmle100.com first so we can try to resolve any problem. USMLE100 may remove posts in Ask the Room that break these rules and may take legal action for false or defamatory statements.\n\n## 23. Code of conduct\n\nUSMLE100 is a professional learning community. In live classes, tutoring, Ask the Room, messages and any USMLE100 group, and towards any student, instructor or staff member, online or offline, you must not:\n\n• harass, bully, threaten, stalk, intimidate or insult anyone;\n\n• post or say anything sexual, obscene, hateful, discriminatory or violent, including about race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, nationality, disability or age;\n\n• contact other students in ways they have not welcomed, or collect or share their personal information;\n\n• disrupt live classes, including through chat, audio, video, inappropriate names or backgrounds;\n\n• advertise, sell, spam or recruit students for other courses, groups or services;\n\n• share or request exam questions, cheat, or encourage others to break any rule;\n\n• pretend to be someone else, or do anything illegal.\n\nUSMLE100 decides at its discretion whether conduct is inappropriate. We may remove messages or posts, remove you from a live class, and suspend or permanently ban your account without refund. We may report threats or illegal conduct to the police. To report a problem, email info@usmle100.com.\n\n## 24. Further disclaimers\n\n• No warranties. The service, content and tools are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, including accuracy, completeness, fitness for a purpose or uninterrupted access. Medical knowledge and exam content change; content may contain errors.\n\n• Not medical advice; no professional relationship. Content is for exam preparation only. It is not medical, legal or career advice and must never be used to diagnose or treat anyone. Using USMLE100 creates no doctor-patient, advisory or employment relationship.\n\n• Third-party services. USMLE100 is not responsible for outages, errors or data incidents at services it relies on, including Zoom, Stripe, Cloudflare, Bunny, Zoho, Calendly or your own internet, device or browser.\n\n• Your responsibility. You are responsible for your exam registration, deadlines, eligibility, visa and licensing requirements, and for checking official exam information with the exam bodies.\n\n• Outside your country. If you use USMLE100 from outside the United States, you are responsible for complying with local laws.\n\n• No personal liability. USMLE100''s owners, instructors, staff and contractors are not personally liable to you; any claim may be brought only against USMLE100 LLC.\n\n• Links. Links to other websites are for convenience; we are not responsible for their content.', '\n', char(10)) WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production') ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value WHERE settings.value = '';
INSERT INTO settings (key, value) SELECT 'privacy_text', replace('Effective November 3, 2026. This policy explains what personal information USMLE100 LLC ("USMLE100") collects through usmle100.com and the student portal, why, and your choices. We do not sell your personal information.\n\n## 1. What we collect\n\n• Name, email, phone number, exam, graduation year — Your account, contacting you, running your program\n\n• Legal name typed as your signature on the Student Agreement — A record that you accepted the agreement\n\n• Payment records (amount, date, status; card details stay with Stripe) — Activating purchases, refunds, disputes, accounting\n\n• Sign-in history, IP address, country, device and browser type, a device cookie — Security: the 2-device limit, unusual-sign-in checks, stopping account sharing\n\n• Viewing records (which lecture, when, how much was watched, session codes) — Viewing limits, resuming where you stopped, tracing leaked recordings\n\n• Study activity (question answers, tests, notes, progress, posts in Ask the Room) — Your progress, performance analytics, the community features\n\n• Messages you send us — Answering you\n\n• Marketing consent (if you opt in) — Sending you USMLE100 news; you can withdraw at any time\n\n## 2. The watermark\n\nYour name, account number and a session code are shown on lecture videos while you watch. This identifies the account a recording or shared copy came from.\n\n## 3. Cookies\n\nWe use only cookies needed to run the site: a sign-in cookie that ends when you close the browser, after 30 minutes of inactivity, or after 24 hours at most, and a device cookie (up to 400 days) that recognises your registered devices. We do not use advertising cookies.\n\n## 4. Who we share information with\n\nWe share information only with providers that run the service for us, under their own privacy and security terms:\n\n• Cloudflare – hosting, database and security\n\n• Stripe – payments\n\n• Bunny.net – lecture video streaming\n\n• Zoom – live classes and tutoring\n\n• Zoho – our business email\n\n• Calendly – booking tutoring sessions\n\n• Email or text-message providers, and our marketing-list provider, only if those features are switched on and, for marketing, only if you opted in\n\nWe may also disclose information if the law requires it, or where reasonably necessary to protect our rights, content or students: for example to a card issuer in a payment dispute, to a platform in a copyright takedown notice, or to our lawyers, an arbitrator or a court in an investigation or legal claim.\n\n## 5. How long we keep it\n\n• Account and study data: while your account is open. If you ask us to delete your account, we remove or anonymise your profile, devices and notes, except records listed below.\n\n• Sign-in history shown to you: 30 days.\n\n• Security and audit records (sign-ins, devices, viewing records, session codes, warnings): up to 2 years.\n\n• Payment records: as long as tax and accounting law requires, even after an account is deleted.\n\n• Records of your agreement (the version you accepted, the box you ticked or payment notice you saw, the legal name you typed, the date, time, IP address and browser): while you have an account and afterwards for as long as a claim about the agreement could be brought.\n\n• Legal holds: if we are investigating suspected misuse, or there is a dispute, chargeback, takedown or legal claim, we keep the records relevant to it until the matter is fully resolved, even if a period above has passed or you ask for deletion.\n\n## 6. Your choices and rights\n\nYou can see your sign-in history and messages in My account. You can ask for a copy of your data, a correction, or deletion of your account at info@usmle100.com. Deleting an account removes or anonymises your personal information; payment records, agreement records and records under a legal hold are kept as described in section 5. You can stop marketing emails at any time.\n\n## 7. Security\n\nWe protect accounts with hashed passwords, sign-in limits, device checks, encrypted connections and passkeys for staff. To protect course content we also monitor viewing as it happens (progress check-ins about every 30 seconds, one lecture at a time, the device limit and unusual sign-ins) and show a visible watermark. Some of these checks are automatic and can pause a viewing or suspend an account until a person reviews it. No system is perfectly secure; tell us at once if you think your account has been misused.\n\n## 8. Age\n\nUSMLE100 is for adults aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.\n\n## 9. Changes and contact\n\nWe will post any change to this policy with its effective date. Questions or requests: info@usmle100.com.', '\n', char(10)) WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production') ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value WHERE settings.value = '';
INSERT INTO settings (key, value) SELECT 'refund_text', replace('Effective November 3, 2026. All sales are final. Please read what each program includes, and the viewing rules, before you buy.\n\n## 1. No refunds\n\nWe do not give refunds for any purchase once payment is complete. This applies to all programs (MedSchool Refresher, Companion, Complete and MAX), Evening Questions, the Course Book, one-on-one tutoring sessions and any additional purchases. It applies whether or not you have started, attended live classes or watched recordings, and whether or not you have used all included tutoring sessions or viewings.\n\n## 2. Limited exceptions\n\nUSMLE100 will refund, in full or in part, only when:\n\n• you were charged more than once for the same purchase by mistake;\n\n• USMLE100 cancels a program before it starts and does not offer you another start date, ends your access for a reason that is not your breach, or fails to deliver a material part of what you bought (such as live classes that are neither held, rescheduled nor recorded) and does not put it right within a reasonable time after you tell us; the refund then covers the unused or undelivered part, in proportion; or\n\n• a refund is required by law.\n\nAny other refund is at USMLE100''s sole discretion and does not create a right to a refund for anyone else.\n\n## 3. What happens if a refund is given\n\nA full refund ends access to what that purchase included, straight away: lectures, recordings, the question bank and other paid features for a program, or Course Book access for a Course Book purchase. Other purchases you made are not affected.\n\n## 4. Chargebacks\n\nPlease contact us at info@usmle100.com before disputing a charge with your bank. If a payment is disputed, access to that purchase is suspended while the dispute is open. If the dispute is decided in our favour, access is restored. A dispute marked as fraudulent may lead to suspension of the whole account.\n\n## 5. Tutoring sessions\n\nOne-on-one sessions are booked through our Calendly scheduling page (calendly.com/usmle100). Sessions are non-refundable. If you cannot attend, contact us at least 24 hours before the session; rescheduling is at our discretion.\n\n## 6. Evening Questions\n\nEvening Questions is sold one month at a time; a month is the next 12 evening classes from your start date. It does not renew automatically: you pay only when you buy another month, so you can stop at any time by not buying the next one. Months already paid are not refunded.\n\n## 7. Contact\n\nQuestions about a charge: info@usmle100.com.', '\n', char(10)) WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production') ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value WHERE settings.value = '';
INSERT INTO settings (key, value) SELECT 'calendly_url', 'https://calendly.com/usmle100/usmle100-1-on-1-tutoring-60mins' WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production') ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value WHERE settings.value = '';
INSERT INTO settings (key, value) SELECT 'contact_email', 'info@usmle100.com' WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production') ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value;
INSERT INTO agreements (title, body, body_hash, material, published_by) SELECT 'USMLE100 Student Content-Protection Agreement', replace('Between USMLE100 LLC ("USMLE100") and the student named below. Effective November 3, 2026.\n\n## 1. Personal use only\n\nI will use USMLE100 lectures, recordings, questions, explanations, the Course Book and all other materials only for my own personal study. My access is personal to me and cannot be transferred, lent or resold.\n\n## 2. No recording or copying\n\nI will not record, screen-record, screenshot, screen-capture, photograph, film, download, save, copy, transcribe in full, or otherwise take or reproduce any lecture, live class, question, explanation, Course Book page or any other content from the website or portal, by any means, including screen-recording software, browser extensions, download tools, a second device or a camera. This applies even if the copy is only for my own personal use.\n\n## 3. No sharing\n\nI will not share, upload, sell, publish or distribute any USMLE100 material, in whole or in part, to any person, website, group chat, file-sharing service or social media.\n\nMy login is mine alone. I will never share my email and password, sign-in codes, passkey or devices with anyone, including family members, friends, classmates or study partners. I will not let anyone else sign in to my account, watch lectures through it, or sit with me to watch them. Sharing my login is a serious breach of this agreement and carries the same consequences as copying content (section 5), including a permanent ban without refund.\n\nOne person, one account. My account is for me only and may never be shared, lent, given, transferred or sold to anyone, for free or for money, for any length of time. I will hold only one USMLE100 account and will not open another account for myself or for anyone else. Account sharing carries the same consequences as copying content (section 5).\n\n## 4. Protections\n\nI understand that:\n\n• my name, account number and a session code are shown on every video I watch, so any copy can be traced to my account;\n\n• my account works on up to 2 registered devices and plays only one lecture at a time;\n\n• viewings, devices, sign-ins and suspected sharing are recorded;\n\n• I must not remove, hide or get around the watermark, viewing limits, device limits, encryption or any other protection, or use any tool that does.\n\n## 5. Consequences\n\n5.1 Strict protection of proprietary materials. All USMLE100 educational materials, including lectures, live sessions, recordings, question banks, explanations, study guides, Course Books, software, website content, graphics, and other proprietary resources, are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Students receive only a limited, personal, revocable, nonexclusive, nontransferable license to access authorized materials for their own educational use. Except where expressly permitted by USMLE100 in writing or required by applicable law, students may not copy, photograph, screenshot, screen-record, download, reproduce, redistribute, transmit, sell, sublicense, publish, upload, or disclose protected materials, in whole or in part, whether for commercial or noncommercial purposes. Students may not share protected content through messaging applications, social media, cloud storage, file-sharing platforms, AI systems, competing educational services, or any other third-party service. Students may not share account credentials, allow unauthorized persons to access their accounts, bypass technical protections, or facilitate unauthorized access by others. These restrictions survive expiration or termination of enrollment.\n\n5.2 Breach, remedies and enforcement costs. Any unauthorized copying, recording, distribution, disclosure, resale, account sharing, or circumvention of security measures is a material breach of this Agreement. USMLE100 may seek a court order stopping the conduct and requiring removal of copies (an injunction), actual damages and any profits from the breach, statutory damages where available under the Copyright Act, and any other remedy the law allows. To the extent a statute, court or arbitrator allows it (for example 17 U.S.C. §§ 505 and 1203), the student will also pay USMLE100''s reasonable attorneys'' fees and costs, and the reasonable, documented investigation, forensic and takedown expenses caused by the breach. This section sets no fixed penalty and does not require a student to pay any fee or cost that applicable law prohibits shifting.\n\n5.3 Disputes. Disputes are resolved as set out in Terms of Service section 20: informal resolution first, individual arbitration with a 30-day opt-out, and court for intellectual-property claims and injunctions (open to both sides). Each party bears its own legal expenses unless a statute, court or arbitrator awards them, as in section 5.2.\n\n5.4 Limitation of liability and protection of business personnel. To the maximum extent permitted by law, USMLE100 provides educational services without guaranteeing examination passage, examination scores, residency placement, professional licensing, or any particular academic or career outcome. USMLE100’s aggregate contractual liability shall not exceed the amount paid by the student during the 12 months preceding the claim, except where applicable law prohibits that limitation. The contracting service provider is USMLE100 LLC. Its owners, members, managers, officers, instructors, employees, and contractors are not personally parties to the student’s service agreement solely by reason of their affiliation with the company. This cap does not apply to USMLE100''s fraud, gross negligence or wilful misconduct, and nothing in this Agreement excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.\n\n5.5 Suspension, termination and evidence. USMLE100 may suspend access immediately and without notice whenever it reasonably suspects unauthorized access, account sharing, copying, recording, redistribution, security circumvention or another material violation. If its review finds in good faith that a violation occurred, USMLE100 may permanently terminate all of the student''s accounts without refund (Terms of Service section 9). USMLE100 may preserve access logs, device records, session information, payment records, watermark evidence and copies of leaked material for investigations, enforcement and legal proceedings, for as long as the matter lasts (Privacy Policy section 5).\n\n5.6 Continuing obligations. Termination, expiration, refund, chargeback, or suspension does not eliminate obligations relating to intellectual-property protection, confidentiality of proprietary course materials, liability for prior breaches, or legally enforceable dispute-resolution provisions. Students must cease unauthorized use and distribution of protected materials following termination and comply with lawful requests to remove unauthorized copies. Sections 1 to 6 and 7a of this Agreement survive termination, expiration, refund or chargeback.\n\nA second detected case of account sharing locks the account until USMLE100 reviews it.\n\nA student can appeal a suspension through My account → Appeals and disputes.\n\n## 6. Ownership\n\nAll materials remain the property of USMLE100 or its licensors. Nothing in this agreement gives me ownership of any material.\n\n## 7. Accuracy and age\n\nThe legal name I type is my true name, and I am at least 18 years old.\n\nI understand that USMLE100 does not guarantee that I will pass any exam or reach any score, and that my exam results alone are not a basis for any claim against USMLE100 (Terms of Service section 11).\n\nI will follow the USMLE100 Code of conduct (Terms section 23). I will treat other students, instructors and staff with respect and will not harass, threaten or behave inappropriately towards anyone. I understand that breaking it can lead to removal from classes and a permanent ban without refund.\n\n## 7a. Further promises\n\n• Live classes: I will not record any live class or tutoring session, and I consent to USMLE100 recording them.\n\n• No AI or bots: I will not use bots, download tools, browser extensions or AI tools to copy, summarise in bulk or extract USMLE100 content, or upload it to any AI service.\n\n• Confidentiality: I will keep all questions, explanations and course materials confidential, during and after my enrollment.\n\n• Evidence: I agree that USMLE100''s viewing, device and sign-in records, and the watermark on any copied material, may be used as evidence that a copy came from my account.\n\n• Responsibility for my account: I am responsible for everything done through my account, unless I reported unauthorised use to USMLE100 straight away.\n\n• Reporting: I will tell USMLE100 at once if I see USMLE100 material shared anywhere or think my account has been used by someone else.\n\n• After my access ends: this agreement continues to apply after my program ends or my account is closed, and I will delete any notes that reproduce course content word for word if asked.\n\n## 8. Other terms\n\nThis agreement is between me and USMLE100 LLC, forms part of the USMLE100 Terms of Service, Refund Policy and Privacy Policy, and is governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina and applicable US federal law. If a court or arbitrator finds any part unenforceable, that part is limited to the extent necessary and the rest still applies.\n\nBy typing my legal name and ticking "I agree", I sign this agreement electronically, with the same effect as a handwritten signature (federal E-SIGN Act; North Carolina Uniform Electronic Transactions Act). USMLE100 keeps a record of the exact version I signed, my typed name, the date and time, and the IP address and browser I signed from, and will send me a copy on request.', '\n', char(10)), '6364a7303fcdb21645ac232bc366c270bc3bdf5de15b3464a7a26d62daab1676', 1, (SELECT id FROM users WHERE is_owner = 1 ORDER BY id LIMIT 1) WHERE EXISTS (